Scientific calculation dependencies remain external packages:
- RDKit (BSD-3-Clause) provides molecule parsing, descriptors, SPS and Bertz CT.
  Its maintained SA_Score implementation retains the Novartis BSD-3-Clause notice.
- BayBE, maintained by Merck (emdgroup), and BoTorch retain their Apache-2.0
  and MIT licenses respectively. Published experimental datasets are not bundled.
- Graph2SMILES network architecture source restored from the publisher's model
  archive retains the existing MIT license in its ASKCOS source directory.
  The matching model weights and vocabulary remain external immutable assets.
- RXNMapper, maintained by IBM RXN / rxn4chemistry, retains its MIT license.
  Its official ALBERT checkpoint remains an external, verified asset. Atom-map
  confidence is not an experimental impurity identification or abundance.
- Open Reaction Database schema code (ord-schema) is Apache-2.0, while its
  deposited reaction datasets are CC-BY-SA-4.0. Full datasets remain external.
  The attributed public reaction projection in tests/fixtures/reactions retains
  CC-BY-SA-4.0; its README identifies the original dataset, authors and changes.

